[gb_boot_start / gb_boot_dispatch]
Ghidra: Reuses the SM83 decoder/analyzer/emitter for the supplied firmware;
no BIOS routine is guessed, replaced or stubbed in the LLE build.
Rationale: A developer build choice selects real BIOS execution or the existing
post-boot HLE. LLE is the default, requires the matching external firmware, starts
at PC 0, routes mapped BIOS addresses before cartridge dispatch, and lets FF50
perform the handoff. BIOS native bodies are produced at build time, including
their SHA-256 identity, without embedding or distributing the raw firmware.

[launcher firmware paths]
Validate picked firmware against the same exact size and SHA-256 as native
dispatch. Remember only per-model paths in the writable state directory; never
copy raw BIOS images. The System panel supports normal LLE startup, including
switching a multi-body game between DMG and CGB modes. Missing cached firmware
prevents skip-launcher startup. HLE builds expose no BIOS runtime selector.
